---
description: Next.js App Router and TypeScript architecture rules
globs: "{app,src}/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Follow `docs/TECHNICAL_SPEC.md`; use App Router and strict TypeScript.
- Default to Server Components. Add `use client` only at the smallest interactive boundary.
- Use Server Actions for same-origin form mutations and Route Handlers for auth, webhooks, uploads, downloads, and external APIs.
- Keep domain logic framework-light in `src/domain`; keep database and secrets server-only.
- Validate external input with schemas and return typed expected errors. Do not throw away authorization or concurrency failures.
- Use Node.js runtime for Neon, Auth.js, Blob, and webhook work unless compatibility is proven.
- Keep build-time module evaluation safe when environment variables are absent.
